Attribution summary (CC BY 3.0 §4(c) / CC BY-SA 2.0 §4(b) / Apache 2.0 §4)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

For every quotation, this repository states: the name of the guide quoted,
its author (Google LLC; for the R guide additionally Hadley Wickham as the
upstream author), a URI for the source, and — through the verbatim /
paraphrase marking described above — whether the wording is the original's or
this repository's. Quoted sentences are unmodified; any modification would be
a defect, not an adaptation. `tools/check_verbatim.py` enforces one part of
this mechanically: a verbatim quote appearing in a newly written block must
already appear, character-for-character after whitespace normalisation, in the
already-source-verified corpus files — so a quote cannot silently drift or be
introduced unsourced. It does not re-check the quotes against the upstream
guides; that remains a human step.


